  "sourceStatement": "For every nonzero real x, (x f′(x) − f(x))/x² = 3x e^(x²), with f(1)=0; find f(2).",
  "freshDerivation": [
    "For x≠0, (f(x)/x)′=(x f′(x)−f(x))/x²=3x e^(x²).",
    "Integrate: f(x)/x=(3/2)e^(x²)+C on the positive interval containing 1 and 2.",
    "Using f(1)=0 gives C=−(3/2)e.",
    "Thus f(2)=2·(3/2)(e⁴−e)=3(e⁴−e)."
  ],
